  "scene": {
    "id": 0,
    "language": "So this note is saying to move to the ball and get possession, uh, when the pass is made. But, um, in- there isn't always a need to move towards the ball, um, because sometimes, uh, the teammate, uh, was able to pass me the ball back, um, without having me move to an open space because the opponent wasn't in between me and the teammate. Um, and then in this situation where it says, \"Pass ball back to teammate at distance form meters,\" um, there's also a situation where, um, I just turned around, uh, received the ball from my teammate, turned around and shot the ball, um, instead of actually passing it back to the teammate because the opponent wasn't in the way of me and the goal, and the opponent was- wasn't really putting pressure on me, um, as a player, um, allowing me to actually turn and shoot. And then finally, um, h- in this note it says, \"Move to the ball and get possession for the final attack,\" after I've already moved, um, in front of my teammate and wh- while my teammate has the ball. So in this situation, there isn't always going to be a need to move towards the ball because now you're already in this advanced position and you're open, in an open space away from the opponent, and you can just stay where you are and receive the ball from where you are. Um, and then after that, you'll be able to turn around and shoot from within 14 meters as stated in the next note.",
